  "mach:judgement": "Assess",
  "mach:judgementReason": "Focused, production-ready Python library (v2.0.9) for drug-name NER — a narrower but complementary scope to general clinical NLP tools like MedCAT. Key differentiators: OMOP concept ID linking (critical for OHDSI/OMOP pipelines), SMILES molecular notation output, and fuzzy matching for pharmaceutical misspellings. MIT licence, pip-installable, actively maintained through 2025. Modest adoption (32 GitHub stars) and no peer-reviewed publication, but fills a specific gap for teams building pharmacovigilance or drug-mention extraction pipelines that need OMOP-ready output.",
  "mach:editorialReviewedAt": "2026-05-12",
